{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DPV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Complexesstack_{X/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-theorem-complexes-algebraic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:51c4750a770cc9fa756cc05653d3a6c80c2a1b1d8fb3cd44b9aae18c6e4f3f2d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:06f952175836c2f88528d4bf7023f91e8677629b870dc96e31ac16a3c26201bf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic spaces which is proper,\nflat, and of finite presentation. Then the stack\n<MATH_0002> parametrizing relatively perfect complexes\nwith vanishing negative self-exts is algebraic. See\nQuot, Theorem <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2d3735c47027e3bc584e41dde56071b1b0383d1040d67b02e9bfecae23fe829d", "unit_id": "tag:0DPV:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DPV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Complexesstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-complexes-diagonal-affine-fp}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8eb490727be49a82a553a6f31562e38a16781f066eda1a3851dd0ab2a512dcb3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f0a96c7bddd4dcf5362f7a51add09e833cac1fc54e0675cec61b93f75ef6f597", "source_text": "The diagonal of <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> is affine\nand of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90699b039ada020b59f55c775c8a69db8b537f658ef6861e5a86d4f2d0fca048", "unit_id": "tag:0DPW:statement"}
